      "side": 1,
      "message": "An exception may happen because some critical state such as the stack is messed up in some way. In this case calling `emergency_write_str` directly, which will hopefully get inlined, seemed somewhat more likely to work than the extra complexity of the format machinery. I suggest at least using `emergency_write_str` once at the start of the exception handler, even if you want to use `eprintln!` after that to print more details, as it\u0027s more helpful for debugging to get at least some idea of what exception happened than a loop of exceptions causing exceptions without managing to log anything.",
